Disclaimer: This is my first review, so please don't judge it too harshly (also, sorry for my bad English!).

   Phasmophobia is a horror game where you explore different locations, encounter various ghosts, and use gear to find evidence in order to identify the ghost. (Pro players manage to identify the ghost without any evidence, but I'm still an average player, so I can't really explain how they do that).

My opinion:
   It's a really interesting and creepy horror game. After some time, you stop being afraid of the ghosts, but there are still moments that can make you scream. It takes determination and curiosity to fully experience and enjoy this game, but believe me, it's so much fun to play with friends! Even solo, it's still exciting! 
   Personally, I have a rather weak PC (somewhere between low and mid-end). However, the game still runs on low settings without any lag. Sorry, I can't say much about the graphics because I'm not the type of person who cares whether it's 4K Ultra or 16x16 pixels.

Advantages:
-Fun to play (and scary as well);A lot (really a lot) of YouTube videos with guides, tutorials, and funny moments, so you can easily find info about things you don't understand;
-Can be played solo or with friends (up to 4 players per lobby, as far as I know);

Disadvantages:
-It could be demanding for low-end PCs (but mine actually manages to run it on minimum settings);
-At some points, it becomes a grind for levels in order to buy better gear (and believe me, you really want better gear as time passes);
-Prestige system — I personally don't hate it, it's cool and works just like it should, but for me, as a person who likes to collect all the badges, getting 10 prestiges is tough. You literally lose everything and can't save anything when you prestige. I really wish they made it so that with every prestige, you could keep one item tier so you don't lose EVERYTHING;
-I haven't encountered any other issues, so that's all from my perspective;

Conclusion:
